        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Mark `text-decoration-skip` as deprecated]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29199</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29199"/>
        <updated>2026-03-06T16:05:59.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">The spec disavows this feature, which I've taken to be functionally a deprecation.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#text-decoration-skipping" rel="nofollow">spec</a> disavows the feature:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The CSSWG resolved to be split skipping functionality into individual properties along the lines of <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-4/#propdef-text-decoration-skip-ink" rel="nofollow">text-decoration-skip-ink</a>, to improve its cascading behavior. See <a href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/843" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/843/hovercard">discussion</a> and <a href="https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/2017Feb/0049.html" rel="nofollow">resolution</a>. This section is a rough draft and has not yet been vetted by the CSSWG</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">An alternative here would be to mark it as non-standard. I don't love that, especially as it implies that we should remove the specification text, which seems silly. I know the guidelines don't intend for us to do something silly, so deprecation seems to capture the spirit of the text better than the letter.</p>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto">Suggested by <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/captainbrosset/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/captainbrosset">@captainbrosset</a> in <a href="https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/3841/changes#r2894674156">https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/3841/changes#r2894674156</a>. Merging this would trigger minting a new, discouraged feature in web-features.</p>

]]></content>
